Q: How do you deal with generated code? A: <pre><code>import subprocess
import os

# Check available python libraries for PDF generation
libs = []
for lib in ['reportlab', 'fpdf', 'fpdf2', 'fitz', 'docx2pdf', 'weasyprint', 'xhtml2pdf', 'pypdf']:
    try:
        __import__(lib)
        libs.append(lib)
    except ImportError:
        pass

print(&quot;Available PDF libraries:&quot;, libs)

# Check if libreoffice is available
try:
    res = subprocess.run([&quot;libreoffice&quot;, &quot;--version&quot;], capture_output=True, text=True)
    print(&quot;LibreOffice version:&quot;, res.stdout.strip())
except Exception as e:
    print(&quot;LibreOffice not available:&quot;, str(e))

# Find available fonts
font_dirs = ['/usr/share/fonts', '/usr/local/share/fonts', '~/.fonts']
fonts = []
for f_dir in font_dirs:
    if os.path.exists(os.path.expanduser(f_dir)):
        for root, dirs, files in os.walk(os.path.expanduser(f_dir)):
            for file in files:
                if file.endswith('.ttf') or file.endswith('.otf'):
                    fonts.append(os.path.join(root, file))

print(f&quot;Found {len(fonts)} fonts in system.&quot;)
# Print some font names to check if we have any Ethiopic or generic Unicode fonts
for f in fonts[:10]:
    print(f)
# Let's search for fonts that might support Ethiopic / Amharic
eth_fonts = [f for f in fonts if any(x in f.lower() for x in ['abyssinica', 'nyala', 'ethiopic', 'amharic', 'dejavu', 'free', 'noto', 'ubuntu', 'liberation', 'unifont'])]
print(f&quot;Found {len(eth_fonts)} potential unicode/ethiopic fonts:&quot;)
for f in eth_fonts[:20]:
    print(f)
# Search specifically for ethiopic Noto fonts
noto_eth = [f for f in fonts if 'ethiopic' in f.lower()]
print(&quot;Noto Ethiopic fonts found:&quot;, noto_eth)
</code></pre>

Q: Alert if a draggable div is not dropped into droppable class A: <p>you can do that by using <code>revert</code> as a function. It gets <code>false</code> when the item is dropped outside a valid droppable, so you can show an alert and return <code>true</code> to move it back.</p>
<pre><code>$('.liveBox').draggable({
    revert: function (droppable) {
        if (!droppable) {
            alert('Please drop the item into a valid area.');
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
});
</code></pre>
<p>Also, <code>revert</code> and <code>containment</code> are options for <code>draggable</code>, not <code>droppable</code>. For the droppable, use:</p>
<pre><code>$('.MDTOptionsHostDiv').droppable({
    accept: '.liveBox'
});
</code></pre>
<p>Since your <code>.liveBox</code> elements are created via AJAX, make sure you initialize <code>draggable()</code> after appending them.</p>
